Subject: Problem invoking MASS lda and S-Plus discrim
Message-ID: <4AB11CD2.8050507@noaa.gov>

I'm running S-Plus 8.1.1 on a Windows XP box.

I can't seem to get the MASS lda function to work. As a test, I used the 
built-in data set "crabs" as follows:

lda(sex ~ FL + RW + CL + CW + BD. data = crabs)

I get back

Problem: Object "sex" not found
Use traceback() to see the call stack

Examining traceback() doesn't tell me much, other than S-Plus doesn't 
recognize any parts of the data frame "crabs." But what really puzzles 
me is that the same thing happens when I type

discrim(sex ~ FL + RW + CL + CW + BD. data = crabs)

I've tried deleting my .Prefs directory and starting over, but that 
doesn't help. the same thing happens under S-Plus 8.0.4. I haven't tried 
going back any further.

Can anyone tell me what gives?

Kim Elmore

