>   The
>   par(new=TRUE) tells the plotting system to forget about the
>   current
>
>   coordinate
>   system (and to forget that anything is plotted on the
>   current
>
>   page).  Omit that line and
>   replace
>
>      plot(density(...),
>   ...)
>
>   with
>
>      lines(density(...))
>
>
>
>   The
>   complete script would be
>
>
>
>
>   hist(mar, nclass = 10,probability =T,
>   xlab = "Number of Mar", ylab = "Proportion of
>   mar",main = "MAR",
> sub = "with normal distribution overlay",
>   density=15)
>
>
>
>   # Density for theoretic normal
>   distribution with same mean
>  lines (density(rnorm(50000,mean(mar),sqrt(var(mar)))))
>
>
>
>
>   Note that
>   the comment is wrong -- that gives you the density
>   of
>
>   a sample
>   from a normal distribution.  To get the actual
>   density
>
>   use the
>   dnorm(x, mean, sd) function, as in
>
>
>
>    x<-seq(min(mar),max(mar),length=500)
>
>    lines(x,
>   dnorm(x,mean(mar),sqrt(var(mar))))
