From: wdunlap at tibco.com (William Dunlap)
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2009 12:52:52 -0700
Subject: Re: Problem with placement of 2nd graph as overlay on graph
In-Reply-To: <CE4C7D1B52D049E5AE4E04174D495754@JansAthlon64>
References: <79144221DAB5416F82F5B5DA50782218@JansAthlon64> <77EB52C6DD32BA4D87471DCD70C8D70001CE5FF9@NA-PA-VBE03.na.tibco.com> <CE4C7D1B52D049E5AE4E04174D495754@JansAthlon64>
Message-ID: <77EB52C6DD32BA4D87471DCD70C8D70001CE600A@NA-PA-VBE03.na.tibco.com>

Use the Poisson density function, dpois(), where 
you

used the normal density function in the other 
example.

You may not want to connect the points where 
the

density is evaluated.   Try the 
following

 

> N<-kyphosis$Number
> hist(N, prob=TRUE, 
breaks=seq(-.5, max(N)+.5, by=1))
> points(pch=16, 0:max(N), 
dpois(0:max(N), mean(N)))
> lines(type="h", 0:max(N), dpois(0:max(N), 
mean(N)))

 

